00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:03,260
Like, should we all just act like dogs chasing bubbles?

163
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:07,380
Well, if we connect this to the bigger picture, the text isn't anti-intellectual.

164
00:14:07,940 --> 00:14:10,120
It's contrasting response latency.

165
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:11,080
Response latency.

166
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:15,720
Right. The time it takes for a system to process a stimulus and react.

167
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:22,820
The human world in this story has massive response latency because everything is mediated by representations.

168
00:14:23,660 --> 00:14:25,920
Maps, ledgers, diplomatic reports.

169
00:14:26,420 --> 00:14:30,740
So when the physical reality diverges from the representation, humans just freeze.

170
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:33,340
The writer freezes because his map is wrong.

171
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:38,040
The landscape has to be perfectly legible before institutions authorize action.

172
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:41,980
Exactly. They demand a global coherence the universe won't provide.

173
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:45,780
But the animals operate on distributed adjustment.

174
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:50,440
The oxen's hooves touch the mud, and the adjustment is instantaneous.

175
00:14:51,020 --> 00:14:53,600
They don't need a global theory of the road to take the next step.

176
00:14:53,740 --> 00:14:55,720
No. They interact directly with reality.

177
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:58,280
But this brings up a massive tension.

178
00:14:58,920 --> 00:15:05,620
If humans are tracked by documents and animals are freed by physical immediacy, where do human stories and identities fit in?

179
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:07,460
Which brings us to the performative domain.

180
00:15:07,460 --> 00:15:09,040
This is where it gets really interesting.

181
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:13,740
Because if administration fails, order is maintained through reiteration with variation.

182
00:15:14,020 --> 00:15:17,060
Right. We go to a market square in Regensburg to see some street theater.

